notes = "FIRST BINDING OBLIGATION IN THIS PROJECT. Everything else so far is CC0.
Shipping without a visible credit for this model is infringement, which makes the
in-game Credits screen a RELEASE BLOCKER rather than polish.

THE REQUIRED NOTICE IS A CONSTRUCTION, NOT A QUOTATION. The Poly Pizza model page
carries no author-supplied attribution string — Sherkiz did not state how they wish
to be credited. The line in required_notice was assembled from creator + title +
licence + source URL per standard CC BY practice. A future reviewer should not read
it as text supplied by the author. If Sherkiz ever publishes a preferred credit
line, it supersedes this.

Full CC BY 3.0 legal code is NOT embedded in license_file: creativecommons.org was
unreachable from the build container at import time. Read the canonical text at
license_url before release.

Aggregator terms resolved 2026-07-20: Poly Pizza's ToS (https://poly.pizza/docs/tos)
layers no additional conditions, stating only that by downloading you agree to
adhere to the Creative Commons licence applying at the time of download. No further
obligation from the aggregator.

Modification status: the .glb in-repo is byte-identical to the upstream download.
Scale (0.72) and the metallic 0.4 -> 0.0 material fix live in Rabbit.tscn, so no
modified copy of the work is distributed in source form. The rendered build does
differ from the original; whether that triggers the CC BY 3.0 s4(b) change-note
requirement is a release-review question, not settled here."
